#. ja: カナールの骨片
#. de: Entenknochen
#. fr: os de canard
#. column 2: piles of duck bones
#. column 8: It is an oft-forgotten fact that Frandelont Raimdelle, famed naturalist, father of modern taxonomy, and author of the Raimdelle Codex, tried multiple times (without success) to classify the common duck─most obviously a cloudkin─as a spoken, believing their incessant quackings to be a highly developed language beyond the comprehension of mankind.
#. column 9: Duck Bones
msgctxt "Item:10119:0:0"
msgid "pile of duck bones"
msgstr "куча утиных костей"

#. de: Entenknochen
#. fr: os de canard
#. column 0: pile of duck bones
#. column 8: It is an oft-forgotten fact that Frandelont Raimdelle, famed naturalist, father of modern taxonomy, and author of the Raimdelle Codex, tried multiple times (without success) to classify the common duck─most obviously a cloudkin─as a spoken, believing their incessant quackings to be a highly developed language beyond the comprehension of mankind.
#. column 9: Duck Bones
msgctxt "Item:10119:0:2"
msgid "piles of duck bones"
msgstr "кучи утиных костей"

#. ja: よい出汁の出る鴨の骨の欠片
#. de: Aus diesen Entenknochen lässt sich eine leckere Brühe herstellen.
#. fr: Ce morceau de la carcasse d'un canard permet de fabriquer un bouillon succulent s'il est longuement bouilli dans l'eau.
#. column 0: pile of duck bones
#. column 2: piles of duck bones
#. column 9: Duck Bones
msgctxt "Item:10119:0:8"
msgid "It is an oft-forgotten fact that Frandelont Raimdelle, famed naturalist, father of modern taxonomy, and author of the Raimdelle Codex, tried multiple times (without success) to classify the common duck─most obviously a cloudkin─as a spoken, believing their incessant quackings to be a highly developed language beyond the comprehension of mankind."
msgstr "Мало кто помнит, что знаменитый натуралист, отец современной систематики и автор «Кодекса Раймделла» Франдэлон Раймделл не раз пытался — и безуспешно — причислить обыкновенную утку, очевидно являющуюся облачным зверем, к разумным существам. Он считал, что её непрестанное кряканье — это высокоразвитый язык, недоступный пониманию людей."

